Z||000011||revin||11-22-2001||11:34 AM||||With a bra on the car is just like bra on a woman. If the two are out in the sun for long periods, paint and body will stay the same color under the bra,while the outside changes color. example: Paint will fade, except under bra. no offence to the ladys!!:P||||reg||1
Z||000012||Phil||11-22-2001||11:49 AM||||The La Bra brand fits much better on the Formula/Coupe anyway. I use a bra only for long trips not for everyday. The way I see it, with the bra you don't get stone chips but you run the risk of scuffing and uneven paint fading, without the bra, you don't get scuffing and uneven fading but you do get stone chips. Also if you show your car some places deduct points if you have one on your car. It all comes down to what you like. If you like the looks of the bra on - GO FOR IT.<P><P>------------------<BR> <BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">     <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000013||Back On Holiday||11-22-2001||11:59 AM||||Never liked bras, but those sport ones are kinda sexy.<P>things cover up  too much, but then again I don't have to wear them cuz I'm a guy.<BR>same with Fiero, I don't think they will need bra's until the fronts start to sag and touch the ground  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||1
